{"id": "EUVD-2026-86879", "enisaUuid": "a61680ba-87d8-3c2b-a7c9-181b7ef7d714", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nbnxt_en: Propagate TPA buffer allocation failures in bnxt_queue_mem_alloc()\n\nbnxt_alloc_one_tpa_info_data() returns -ENOMEM as soon as one allocation\nfails. This leaves the remaining rxr->rx_tpa[] entries zeroed.\n\nbnxt_queue_mem_alloc() discards that return value, so the partially\ninitialized ring is installed by bnxt_queue_start().\n\nSince the agg_id is picked by the hardware and bnxt_alloc_agg_idx maps\nit to a SW index in rxr->rx_tpa[], it is possible that an uninitialized\nslot can be chosen which would hand a zero DMA address to the device.\n\nFix this by checking the return value of bnxt_alloc_one_tpa_info_data\nand unwinding, freeing the ring buffers.", "datePublished": "2026-09-25T10:21:56", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:09:33", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d7db2e4953e4626339fd0075564a3e447650d37b", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c8050386a2209b2a474c1eb4bd1574dc19129bfb", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/37e08dc821a57fe0592c917486b638caa888b46d", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b814dfbfeb0a68c9a52073f2caa05a2d5247a329"], "aliases": ["GHSA-5rwh-p838-cqxj", "CVE-2026-97571"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.2, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "276b6c33-1c18-3d04-8ada-bad3275cb922", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "490e6511-8e23-38cf-8d6c-92216ffe150f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "4cac3cc6-b60f-302e-b9d6-cac82917e60f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "bd649c5cc958169b8a8a3e77ea926d92d472b02a <b814dfbfeb0a68c9a52073f2caa05a2d5247a329"}, {"id": "5f5b9a71-9d34-31f4-9abd-4219be1564f8", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.53"}, {"id": "6466599e-7625-3c52-9d13-067a3ba1c080", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.7"}, {"id": "967da506-348e-31ba-80f1-4234c2413834", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.13"}, {"id": "b17e3fba-9558-3f22-af01-3be025ff4e52", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "0997443906b96a051011f220a61e6dce4602ec54 <d7db2e4953e4626339fd0075564a3e447650d37b"}, {"id": "b81fda0a-edce-3471-839d-de95a64b25e7", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "bd649c5cc958169b8a8a3e77ea926d92d472b02a <c8050386a2209b2a474c1eb4bd1574dc19129bfb"}, {"id": "bbec79f7-dca6-30fa-8cb2-179e00934daa", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "bd649c5cc958169b8a8a3e77ea926d92d472b02a <37e08dc821a57fe0592c917486b638caa888b46d"}, {"id": "d7034481-8920-3786-af0f-8f5194a074bc", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.12.20 <6.12.112"}, {"id": "e300f00e-ccc0-36b0-b632-de65dc76e418", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.112"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "83ece600-e9c7-327d-8b1f-432806d46e63", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}